    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a gross reserve strengthening of $57.60 million for prior underwriting years, calculated from the gross claims development triangle and impacting underwriting years from 2012 to 2019. The overall results for 2021 were impacted by current year weather-related large loss events such as Hurricane Ida, Winter Storm Uri, and PCS 2176 Wind and Thunderstorm. Prior year results (2020) were affected by Hurricane Laura, Hurricane Sally, PCS 2016 Wind and Thunderstorm, and the Coronavirus Pandemic, as well as the purchase of an Adverse Development Cover for 2017 and prior underwriting years.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "Gross technical provisions have increased to $2,493.5m from $2,215.2m. This includes an increase in unearned premiums and claims outstanding, principally as IBNR, attributed to increased gross premiums in the year.",
      "Reserve risk is the risk that claims and claim expense reserves subsequently prove to be insufficient to cover eventual claims. Deterioration in reserves can originate from frequency of claims being more than expected, severity of claims being higher than expected and difference between timing of claims payments versus expected.",
      "Gross claims incurred comprise the estimated cost of all claims occurring during the year, whether reported or not, including claims handling costs and adjustments to claims outstanding from previous years.",
      "The provision for claims and claim expenses includes estimates for unpaid claims and claim expenses on reported losses as well as an estimate of losses incurred but not reported (\"IBNR\")."
